## Architecture Decisions

### Standalone Architecture

This project uses Angular 21 standalone components — no NgModules. All components, directives, and pipes declare their dependencies via the `imports` array in their `@Component` decorator.

### Folder Structure

- `platform/` owns shell, authentication, administration, shared infrastructure and public contracts.
- `domains/<id>/` owns portable business routes, services, models and tests.
- `.generated/` holds deterministic lazy registration outside the platform.
- Root app files forward to platform composition roots for Angular tooling.

See [DomainPortability.md](DeveloperReference/DomainPortability.md) for the V1 contract and compatibility prerequisites.

### Routing Strategy

- Lazy-loaded feature routes via `loadComponent` / `loadChildren`
- Route guards for authentication enforcement
- Wildcard catch-all for unmatched URLs

### Error Handling Strategy

- Global `ErrorHandler` captures unhandled exceptions
- HTTP `errorInterceptor` handles API response errors (401, 403, 5xx)
- Structured logging via `LoggerService` with environment-aware level suppression

### Security

- Content Security Policy via `<meta>` tag in `index.html`
{{ if model.angular_cognito_enabled }}
- Cognito sign-in: authorization code + PKCE, state and nonce checks, no client secret (see AUTHENTICATION.md)
- Auth interceptor attaches Bearer tokens only to the configured API (parsed origin and path)
- Missing or invalid runtime configuration fails closed
- Route guards prevent unauthorized navigation
{{ else }}
- Authentication disabled: all generated routes are public
{{ end }}
{{ if model.manifest.ui_targets | array.contains "mobile" }}

### Mobile Strategy

- Ionic Angular for UI components and native-like UX
- Capacitor for native platform access (Android/iOS)
- PlatformService for runtime platform detection
- Adaptive layouts based on platform context
{{ end }}
